Taking a waiting thread's process stops it but leaves it on the notification's waiters,
so a signal would wake a thread that has no process to run in,
and a destroy of the thread's pool would leave the ring leading into memory that is no longer a thread;
a notification queues only the threads waiting on it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: queue holds a thread it is not for
Report: runnable thread waits on something

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -273,9 +273,6 @@ void sched_unbind(struct cap *bound)
 void sched_unhost(struct cap *hosted)
 {
     struct thread *t = hosted_thread(hosted);
-    if (t->state == THREAD_WAITING) {
-        unwait(t);
-    }
     t->state = THREAD_STOPPED;
     *hosted = (struct cap){ 0 };
     thread_settle(t);
